From 02ec42b0cb96fa1a89a850f9c484c3dc5a42ffb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 08:45:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add AltiVec needle and string search

Vectorizes the remaining search paths on AltiVec: advance_pattern_pin1_pma,
advance_pattern_pin2..8_one and _pma, advance_chars and advance_chars_pma,
and advance_string and advance_string_pma.

The hot path tests the whole compare mask with simd_mask_any(), a single
record form compare and a branch on CR6. Only on a match does
ADV_ALTIVEC_SCAN store the mask and walk its bytes, so the store stays off
the common path. The macro is endian aware so the same source works when
built for VSX/little endian. Both lvsl load controls are hoisted out of
each loop since the streams advance by 16 bytes.

advance_string and advance_string_pma delegate to routines the way the NEON
path does.

pattern.cpp now treats AltiVec like NEON when choosing search strategy:
pinmax 8 and freqmax3 160 (VMX is 128 bit, so pins above 8 are not
supported), the needle frequency threshold, and no forcing of Boyer-Moore
now that a 128 bit SIMD filter is available.

Verified with the full ugrep test suite, single and multi threaded, under
qemu-ppc -cpu 7400 (G4, AltiVec without VSX, so any accidental VSX
instruction traps).  Also cross checked against GNU grep on a 2.2MB corpus
over 63 runs driving pin counts 1 to 8, multi-char literals and the string
paths, with counts and full -no output byte identical.

